# narc rules

narc ships 12 rules. Every finding names its rule; `narc explain <rule>` prints the same documentation in your terminal.

| Severity | Verdict | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 🔴 error | BUSTED | High-confidence integrity violation. Fails `narc scan` and blocks agents by default. |
| 🟡 warning | SUSPICIOUS | Often a cheat, sometimes legitimate: needs a human look. |
| 🔵 info | NOTE | Worth knowing. Never fails a build by default. |

Change a rule's severity, or turn it off, under `rules:` in `.narc.yml` (for example `any-cast: error` or `retry-added: off`).

## Index

| Rule | Severity | Category | Summary |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| [`skip-added`](#skip-added) | 🔴 error | tests | New skip/disable markers (`it.skip`, `xit`, `@pytest.mark.skip`, `t.Skip`, `#[ignore]`, `@Disabled`). |
| [`focus-added`](#focus-added) | 🔴 error | tests | `.only`, `fit`, `fdescribe`: silently skips every other test in the file. |
| [`assertion-weakened`](#assertion-weakened) | 🟡 warning | tests | A specific matcher was replaced by a weaker one (`toEqual(x)` → `toBeDefined()`), or a tolerance was widened. |
| [`assertions-removed`](#assertions-removed) | 🔴 error | accounting | A surviving test lost assertions (`3 → 1`). |
| [`test-file-deleted`](#test-file-deleted) | 🟡 warning | accounting | A test file was deleted and its tests were not re-added elsewhere. |
| [`any-cast`](#any-cast) | 🟡 warning | escapes | `as any`, `as unknown as T`, `<any>`, `cast(Any, ...)` (info in tests). |
| [`lint-suppressed`](#lint-suppressed) | 🟡 warning | escapes | `eslint-disable`, `# noqa`, `//nolint`, `#[allow(...)]`, `@SuppressWarnings` (info in tests). |
| [`hardcoded-answer`](#hardcoded-answer) | 🟡 warning | escapes | Source special-cases a literal that the tests use as input or expected output. |
| [`ci-failure-ignored`](#ci-failure-ignored) | 🔴 error | ci | `continue-on-error: true`, `allow_failure: true`, `\|\| true` on a verification command. |
| [`coverage-lowered`](#coverage-lowered) | 🔴 error | ci | Coverage thresholds were lowered or removed. |
| [`protected-path`](#protected-path) | 🔴 error | integrity | A file matching a `protected:` glob in .narc.yml was modified or deleted. |
| [`waiver-missing-reason`](#waiver-missing-reason) | 🟡 warning | integrity | A narc:allow comment must say why the waived change is acceptable. |

## Tests

### skip-added

**Test skipped** · 🔴 `error` · category `tests`

New skip/disable markers (`it.skip`, `xit`, `@pytest.mark.skip`, `t.Skip`, `#[ignore]`, `@Disabled`).

A skipped test cannot fail, so skipping a failing test hides the bug instead of fixing it.

Bad:

```ts
it.skip('rejects expired tokens', async () => {
  expect(await verify(expired)).toBe(false)
})
```

Good: fix `verify()` so the test passes. narc recognizes:

- `it.skip`, `describe.skip`, `xit`, `xdescribe` (Jest, Vitest, Mocha)
- `@pytest.mark.skip` and `pytest.skip()` (pytest)
- `t.Skip()` (Go), `#[ignore]` (Rust), `@Disabled` (JUnit)

See [the waiver guide](https://github.com/huyth45/narc#waivers) when a skip is **really** intended.

**How to fix:** Fix the code under test so the test passes instead of skipping it. If the test itself is wrong, fix the test and say why in the commit.

**Waive** (only with a reason): `narc:allow skip-added reason="..."` in a comment on or above the line, or an `allow:` entry in `.narc.yml`.

### focus-added

**Test focused** · 🔴 `error` · category `tests`

`.only`, `fit`, `fdescribe`: silently skips every other test in the file.

**How to fix:** Remove the focus marker so the whole suite runs.

**Waive** (only with a reason): `narc:allow focus-added reason="..."` in a comment on or above the line, or an `allow:` entry in `.narc.yml`.

### assertion-weakened

**Assertion weakened** · 🟡 `warning` · category `tests`

A specific matcher was replaced by a weaker one (`toEqual(x)` → `toBeDefined()`), or a tolerance was widened.

**How to fix:** Keep the precise assertion and fix the code until it holds.

**Waive** (only with a reason): `narc:allow assertion-weakened reason="..."` in a comment on or above the line, or an `allow:` entry in `.narc.yml`.

## Accounting

### assertions-removed

**Assertions removed** · 🔴 `error` · category `accounting`

A surviving test lost assertions (`3 → 1`).

**How to fix:** Restore the removed assertions; if one is obsolete, replace it with an assertion about the new behavior.

**Waive** (only with a reason): `narc:allow assertions-removed reason="..."` in a comment on or above the line, or an `allow:` entry in `.narc.yml`.

### test-file-deleted

**Test file deleted** · 🟡 `warning` · category `accounting`

A test file was deleted and its tests were not re-added elsewhere.

**How to fix:** Keep the tests, or move them to the file that now covers this code.

**Waive** (only with a reason): `narc:allow test-file-deleted reason="..."` in a comment on or above the line, or an `allow:` entry in `.narc.yml`.

## Escapes

### any-cast

**Type escape (any cast)** · 🟡 `warning` · category `escapes`

`as any`, `as unknown as T`, `<any>`, `cast(Any, ...)` (info in tests).

**How to fix:** Fix the types instead of casting them away.

**Waive** (only with a reason): `narc:allow any-cast reason="..."` in a comment on or above the line, or an `allow:` entry in `.narc.yml`.

### lint-suppressed

**Lint rule suppressed** · 🟡 `warning` · category `escapes`

`eslint-disable`, `# noqa`, `//nolint`, `#[allow(...)]`, `@SuppressWarnings` (info in tests).

**How to fix:** Fix the lint error instead of silencing it.

**Waive** (only with a reason): `narc:allow lint-suppressed reason="..."` in a comment on or above the line, or an `allow:` entry in `.narc.yml`.

### hardcoded-answer

**Hardcoded test answer** · 🟡 `warning` · category `escapes`

Source special-cases a literal that the tests use as input or expected output.

**How to fix:** Implement the general logic; the tests should pass for inputs they do not mention.

**Waive** (only with a reason): `narc:allow hardcoded-answer reason="..."` in a comment on or above the line, or an `allow:` entry in `.narc.yml`.

## CI

### ci-failure-ignored

**CI failure ignored** · 🔴 `error` · category `ci`

`continue-on-error: true`, `allow_failure: true`, `|| true` on a verification command.

**How to fix:** Let the step fail and fix what makes it fail.

**Waive** (only with a reason): `narc:allow ci-failure-ignored reason="..."` in a comment on or above the line, or an `allow:` entry in `.narc.yml`.

### coverage-lowered

**Coverage threshold lowered** · 🔴 `error` · category `ci`

Coverage thresholds were lowered or removed.

**How to fix:** Restore the threshold and add tests for the uncovered code.

**Waive** (only with a reason): `narc:allow coverage-lowered reason="..."` in a comment on or above the line, or an `allow:` entry in `.narc.yml`.

## Integrity

### protected-path

**Protected file changed** · 🔴 `error` · category `integrity`

A file matching a `protected:` glob in .narc.yml was modified or deleted.

**How to fix:** Revert the change to the protected file. If it really must change, a human should make or approve that change.

**Waive** (only with a reason): `narc:allow protected-path reason="..."` in a comment on or above the line, or an `allow:` entry in `.narc.yml`.

### waiver-missing-reason

**Waiver without a reason** · 🟡 `warning` · category `integrity`

A narc:allow comment must say why the waived change is acceptable.

**How to fix:** Add a reason: narc:allow <rule> reason="why this is fine (link to issue)"
